Sounds like the 1.5T model will be available in July and the 2T model in August.

@elonmusk: "In addition to their excellent and unique training data, the Cursor team is also making major engineering contributions to v9 SFT and RL. It’s an honor and a pleasure to work with them."

For the 1.5T run, Cursor data was added in supplemental training, which is not quite as good as having it in initial training. The 2T run, which started a few weeks ago, has greatly improved data scope and scale in almost every arena, along with many upgrades and fixes to the training recipe. That will finish in late July for an August release.

Our internal assessment is that Grok 4.5 is roughly comparable to Opus 4.7, but much faster. The combination of capability, faster speed, and lower cost makes it competitive.

We are focusing on real-world usefulness, not just benchmarks. Engineers at Tesla and SpaceX find Grok 4.5 genuinely useful, which is what truly matters.

